			"Message": "build(Rest): Rebuild binary after OXC migration and compiler features\n\nThis commit updates the pre-compiled Rest binary to reflect the recent architectural changes:\n\n- OXC compiler migration (replacing SWC with Oxidation Compiler ecosystem)\n- New `compile` subcommand for standalone TypeScript compilation\n- Phase 3 build features (NLS processing, Worker compilation, Bundle system)\n\nThe binary was rebuilt using the latest OXC toolchain, incorporating the memory safety fixes in the compiler pipeline and the new NPM packaging for `@codeeditorland/rest`. This ensures the CLI matches the source code state after the significant refactoring in recent commits.\n\nRefs: be30545f8a18282c825875f08cb4c75d93ae6545",
			"SHA": "150547b7302c5c08402cec0077c90f41193d8425"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-03-11T02:31:46Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⡇⠀⠀",
				87,
				44
			],
			"Message": "feat(Rest): Migrate from SWC to OXC compiler ecosystem\n\nThis commit replaces the SWC (Speedy Web Compiler) with OXC (Oxidation Compiler), a modern Rust-based JavaScript/TypeScript toolchain that provides 10-100x speedup over traditional TypeScript compilers.\n\n## Key Changes\n\n### Compiler Migration (SWC → OXC)\n- **Cargo.toml**: Replaced all `swc_*` workspace dependencies with `oxc_*` crates:\n  - `oxc_allocator`, `oxc_parser`, `oxc_transformer`, `oxc_minifier`\n  - `oxc_codegen`, `oxc_semantic`, `oxc_span`, `oxc_ast`\n- **New OXC modules**: Created `Source/Fn/OXC/` with full compiler implementation:\n  - `Parser.rs`: Ultra-fast TypeScript parsing with ESTree compatibility\n  - `Transformer.rs`: AST transformation with TypeScript, JSX support\n  - `Codegen.rs`: Efficient code generation from AST\n  - `Compiler.rs`: Main orchestration with memory safety fixes\n  - `Compile.rs` & `Watch.rs`: Compilation entry and file watching\n\n### Critical Fixes\n- **Segfault Fix**: Resolved memory safety issue in `Compiler::compile_file_to()` by ensuring allocator stays alive in a dedicated scope until after code generation completes. The original bug occurred when program was moved out of ParseResult, causing use-after-free when the allocator was dropped prematurely.\n- **Nightly Rust**: Removed `-Zshare-generics=y` from `.cargo/config.toml` as it's nightly-only and incompatible with stable Rust.\n\n### NPM Package Support\nAdded full NPM packaging for `@codeeditorland/rest`:\n- `package.json`: Package manifest with platform-specific optional dependencies\n- `bin/Rest.js`: CLI wrapper script\n- `postinstall.js`: Platform detection and binary installation script\n- `prepublishOnly.sh`: Cross-platform build script for publishing\n\n### Documentation Updates\n- Updated `README.md` to reflect OXC stack instead of SWC\n- Added OXC compilation flow diagrams and architecture explanation\n- Deleted obsolete `Documentation/Rust` submodule\n\n### Code Quality\n- Improved code formatting and style consistency across all modules\n- Added comprehensive `tracing::instrument` attributes for diagnostic logging\n- Maintained backward-compatible `Source/Fn/SWC/` module that wraps OXC\n\nThis migration enables the Rest element to leverage OXC's high-performance compiler for bundling VS Code platform code from Dependency submodules for use by the Cocoon extension host.",
			"SHA": "be30545f8a18282c825875f08cb4c75d93ae6545"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-03-05T21:58:46Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				74,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Rest): Add compile subcommand for standalone TypeScript compilation\n\nThis commit introduces a new `compile` subcommand to the Rest CLI, enabling it to function as a standalone TypeScript compiler that outputs to a specified directory rather than in-place.\n\nKey changes:\n- Added `compile` subcommand in `Binary/Command.rs` with flags for input/output directories, target ES version, module format, source maps, and VSCode compatibility options\n- Created `Fn/SWC/Compile.rs` module that uses walkdir to discover TypeScript files and compiles them while preserving directory structure\n- Updated `Struct/SWC.rs` with new `compile_file_to` method for writing compiled output to specific paths\n- Modified decorator configuration to use `legacy: true` for better VSCode compatibility\n- Added `use_define_for_class_fields` option to align with VSCode's default behavior (false)\n\nThe implementation supports VSCode build pipeline requirements by providing flexible compilation options including tree-shaking, module format conversion (ESM/CommonJS), and proper decorator handling needed for the Cocoon extension host.",
			"SHA": "789d672b1da7ca566850b39220ea74ae9127c02f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-03-05T17:32:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡟⠀⠀⠀",
				70,
				25
			],
			"Message": "feat(Rest): Implement Phase 3 advanced build features\n\nThis commit adds significant build tooling capabilities to the Rest element for the Land project's VSCode-compatible build pipeline.\n\n## New Modules Added\n\n### Bundle System (`Source/Fn/Bundle/`)\n- `BundleBuilder`: Orchestrates the bundling process with support for single-file, multi-file, and watch modes\n- `BundleConfig`: Comprehensive configuration for bundler (output, minification, tree-shaking, source maps, externals)\n- `EsbuildWrapper`: Optional integration for complex builds that Rest can't handle alone\n\n### NLS Processing (`Source/Fn/NLS/`)\n- `NLSExtractor`: Extracts localization keys from TypeScript source (supports nls.localize, localize, localize2 patterns)\n- `NLSBundle`: Generates and manages localization bundles for different languages\n- `NLSReplacer`: Replaces NLS keys with actual localized strings at build time\n\n### Worker Compilation (`Source/Fn/Worker/`)\n- `WorkerDetector`: Detects worker files by naming conventions and content markers\n- `WorkerBootstrap`: Generates bootstrap code for module, classic, and shared workers\n- `WorkerCompiler`: Orchestrates worker compilation with dependency extraction\n\n### Transform System (`Source/Fn/Transform/`)\n- `PrivateFieldTransform`: Converts TypeScript private fields (#field) to regular properties (__field) for VSCode compatibility\n\n### Advanced Compiler Config (`Source/Struct/CompilerConfig.rs`)\n- Consolidates all Phase 3 feature configurations (NLS, Worker, Bundle)\n- Supports multiple compilation modes: SingleFile, Bundle, Worker, VSCode\n\n## Existing File Updates\n- `Source/Struct/SWC.rs`: Added ModuleFormat enum, TreeShaking, Minify support; updated default target to ES2024\n- `Cargo.toml`: Added `tempfile` workspace dependency for worker compilation tests\n\nThese features enable the Rest element to perform full VSCode build pipeline operations, bundling VS Code platform code from Dependency submodules for use by the Cocoon extension host.",
			"SHA": "028923579dbe498d2cf9ea3ca803aa125b9d39ae"
		},
